def recovery():
    d=base('grow_recovery_methods_workshop','The recovery methods workshop','Choose a method by the mixture and the substance you need','Choose and justify filtration, evaporation or evaporation with condensation for a stated recovery target.',7,['Distinguish dissolving from melting.','Know that a solution contains a dissolved substance and a solvent.'],['Identify the mixture and desired recovered substance.','Explain what passes through a filter and what remains.','Sequence a recovery route and account for each component.'],[('filtration','Separating an insoluble solid from a fluid using a filter.'),('residue','Material left on the filter.'),('filtrate','Fluid that passes through a filter.'),('evaporation','Liquid changing to gas at its surface.'),('condensation','Gas changing to liquid.'),('recovery target','The substance or substances that a method is intended to collect.')],['Shared mixture/target cards, selected route, pencils; optional sequencing tokens.'],['Default lesson is a process simulation and paper investigation. No heated separation apparatus is used.','Name the target before choosing a method. The model follows sand, salt and water; it does not certify drinking-water purity.'],['Do not heat, boil, distil or taste any classroom mixture as part of this pack.','The evaporation/condensation diagram is a schematic of processes, not an apparatus construction guide.','Optional physical filtration would require a separately prepared school method; all necessary evidence is already supplied.'],'Use the four recovery briefs and process cards. Screen process choices and paper sequencing both provide the complete investigation.',[('A filter removes dissolved salt from water.','Dissolved salt passes with water through ordinary filter paper; sand can be retained.','Ask where the salt appears after filtering.'),('Evaporation automatically gives collected liquid water.','Open evaporation lets water vapour escape; collecting water requires capture and condensation.','Ask where the target water ends up.'),('One separation method works for every mixture and target.','The method depends on component properties and what you want to collect.','Compare saltwater target salt with saltwater target water.')],['Match mixture/target pairs to process cards.','Explain four routes and account for components.','Evaluate multistep recovery, loss and limits of purity claims.'],[RSC,RSC2,source('Royal Society of Chemistry: Evaporation, filtration and crystallisation','https://edu.rsc.org/cpd/evaporation-filtration-and-crystallisation-teaching-practical-science/3009017.article','Checked September 2026. Separation teaching and target-dependent methods. This resource supplies a non-heated paper alternative.')])
